IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lga-rates`

-- Local Government Act 1995 (WA), Part 6 Division 6 (rates) -- worked cases, from the seat of the ratepayer.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked against
-- a decided case, a council's rate notice or the Local Government (Financial Management) Regulations 1996 (not deposited).
-- Valuations, rates in the dollar, minimum payments, charges and interest rates are ILLUSTRATIVE inputs.
--
-- Generated by the scratchpad script gen_wa_local-government-act-1995_baseline.py. Expected results were written by hand from the text.
--
-- The lives. c055 (2029-07-15): Chloe and Liam take handover of their new house in Byford; the lot was bought vacant
-- (settled 15 May 2028). d084 (2064-01-15): Daniel (67) and Priya (66) pay council rates on their Nedlands home. Daniel draws
-- no Age Pension; whether either holds an entitlement under the Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 is
-- not decided here and is asked both ways.

§ `s 6.26 -- rateable land`

-- c055 / d084: a home is rateable land (s 6.26(1))
#ASSERT `Is my land rateable` `a privately owned home`
-- c055: the Byford lot before the house was built
#ASSERT `Is my land rateable` `a privately owned vacant lot`
-- s 6.26(2)(a)
#ASSERT NOT `Is my land rateable` `Crown land used or held for a public purpose, or unoccupied`
-- s 6.26(2)(g)
#ASSERT NOT `Is my land rateable` `land used exclusively for charitable purposes`

-- s 6.53(c)
#ASSERT `How much of the year's rates must I pay for land that became rateable` 3650 146 365 EQUALS 1460

§ `ss 6.43-6.55 -- who must pay`

-- d084: Daniel and Priya, owners in possession of the Nedlands house (s 6.44(1))
#ASSERT `Am I liable to pay the rates` TRUE

-- d084: two owners are jointly and severally liable (s 6.44(2))
#ASSERT `Can I be made to pay all the rates on land I own with others` 2
#ASSERT NOT `Can I be made to pay all the rates on land I own with others` 1

-- a buyer who takes title while rates are unpaid (s 6.55(1)(ii))
#ASSERT `Can the rates be recovered from me` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Can the rates be recovered from me` FALSE FALSE

-- c055 background: the Byford lot bought on 15 May 2028, s 6.52(1)(a)
#ASSERT `What share of the year's rates is mine as buyer` 1830 366 47 EQUALS 235

§ `s 6.28 -- the valuation`

-- d084: Nedlands, taken as determined on gross rental value (ASSUMED; the Gazette notice is not deposited)
#ASSERT `On what valuation is my land rated` `gross rental value determined` FALSE EQUALS `gross rental value`
-- c055: Byford house, non-rural use, determination unknown: conditional answer (s 6.28(2)(b))
#ASSERT `On what valuation is my land rated` `not known to me` FALSE EQUALS `gross rental value, if the Minister's determination follows the general principle`
-- a farm, determination unknown (s 6.28(2)(a))
#ASSERT `On what valuation is my land rated` `not known to me` TRUE EQUALS `unimproved value, if the Minister's determination follows the general principle`
-- the determination governs even against the general principle (s 6.28(1))
#ASSERT `On what valuation is my land rated` `unimproved value determined` FALSE EQUALS `unimproved value`

-- c055: an interim valuation after the house is completed (s 6.28(5)(a))
#ASSERT `Which valuation are my rates worked out on` TRUE EQUALS `the interim, amended or new valuation made during the year`
-- d084: no change during 2063/64 (s 6.28(4))
#ASSERT `Which valuation are my rates worked out on` FALSE EQUALS `the valuation in force on 1 July`

§ `ss 6.32, 6.33, 6.35, 6.36 -- how much`

-- d084: Nedlands, illustrative GRV $80,000 at 7c in the dollar = $5,600, above the minimum
#ASSERT `How much are my general rates` 80000 0.07 1400 EQUALS 5600
-- c055: the Byford lot while vacant, illustrative GRV $9,000 at 10c = $900, so the $1,500 minimum (s 6.35(1))
#ASSERT `How much are my general rates` 9000 0.1 1500 EQUALS 1500
-- c055: the Byford house after the interim valuation, illustrative GRV $26,000 at 10c = $2,600
#ASSERT `How much are my general rates` 26000 0.1 1500 EQUALS 2600

-- c055: the vacant lot
#ASSERT `Am I paying the minimum payment` 9000 0.1 1500
-- c055: the house
#ASSERT NOT `Am I paying the minimum payment` 26000 0.1 1500

-- c055: $2,600 + an illustrative $350 service charge
#ASSERT `What is the total of my rates and service charges` 26000 0.1 1500 0 350 EQUALS 2950

-- more than twice the lowest, no Minister's approval (s 6.33(3))
#ASSERT NOT `Is my differential rate within the limit` 0.12 0.05 FALSE
-- exactly twice the lowest is within the limit
#ASSERT `Is my differential rate within the limit` 0.1 0.05 FALSE

-- s 6.36(3)(b)(ii)
#ASSERT `How many days do I have to make a submission` 0 EQUALS 21

§ `ss 6.33(4), 6.40 -- changes during the year`

-- c055: the interim valuation changes the rateable value (s 6.40(1)(a))
#ASSERT `Must my rates be reassessed` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- only the differential characteristics changed (s 6.33(4))
#ASSERT NOT `Must my rates be reassessed` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- the land became rateable (s 6.40(1)(b))
#ASSERT `Must my rates be reassessed` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Must my rates be reassessed` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- s 6.40(3)(a)(i)
#ASSERT `Do I get a refund of overpaid rates` 2600 2200 TRUE EQUALS `a refund, because I asked for one`
-- s 6.40(3)(a)
#ASSERT `Do I get a refund of overpaid rates` 2600 2200 FALSE EQUALS `a refund or a credit against future rates, as the local government chooses`

§ `ss 6.41, 6.45, 6.50 -- when due, and instalments`

-- c055: notice issued 1 August 2029, due 5 September: 35 days (s 6.50(2))
#ASSERT `Is my due date lawful` 20290801 20290905
-- c055 variant: due 4 September, 34 days
#ASSERT NOT `Is my due date lawful` 20290801 20290904
-- d084: Nedlands 2063/64 notice, 36 days
#ASSERT `Is my due date lawful` 20630801 20630906

-- c055: the notice after reassessment (s 6.45(2))
#ASSERT `How may I pay my rates` TRUE EQUALS `a single payment, or the instalments remaining this year`
-- d084: the ordinary notice (s 6.45(1))
#ASSERT `How may I pay my rates` FALSE EQUALS `a single payment, or 4 instalments, or another instalment plan in the budget`

-- d084: ($5,600 + an illustrative $20 instalment charge) / 4
#ASSERT `How much is each instalment` 5600 20 FALSE EQUALS 1405
-- d084 variant: entitled to a rebate or deferment, so no instalment charge (s 6.51(4)(b))
#ASSERT `How much is each instalment` 5600 20 TRUE EQUALS 1400

-- two months to the day, across the year end (s 6.50(3))
#ASSERT `Is this instalment due date lawful` 20291205 20300205
#ASSERT NOT `Is this instalment due date lawful` 20291205 20300204

-- 28 days before the instalment (s 6.41(2)(b))
#ASSERT `Was my instalment notice early enough` 20291008 20291105
-- 27 days
#ASSERT NOT `Was my instalment notice early enough` 20291009 20291105

§ `s 6.51 -- interest, and the rebates connection`

-- d084: resolved, overdue, no rebate or deferment entitlement
#ASSERT `Does interest run on my overdue rates` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- d084 variant: entitled to a rebate or deferment under the 1992 Act: no interest (s 6.51(4)(a))
#ASSERT NOT `Does interest run on my overdue rates` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- no resolution at the time of imposing (s 6.51(1))
#ASSERT NOT `Does interest run on my overdue rates` FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- paid by the due date
#ASSERT NOT `Does interest run on my overdue rates` TRUE FALSE FALSE

-- budget above the illustrative prescribed maximum (s 6.51(2))
#ASSERT `What is the highest interest rate I can be charged` 12 11 EQUALS 11

-- $1,000 overdue 30 days at 7.3% (simple daily interest ASSUMED)
#ASSERT `About how much interest will I be charged` 1000 7.3 11 20300205 20300307 TRUE FALSE EQUALS 6
-- d084 variant: entitled to a rebate or deferment
#ASSERT `About how much interest will I be charged` 1000 7.3 11 20300205 20300307 TRUE TRUE EQUALS 0
-- paid before the due date
#ASSERT `About how much interest will I be charged` 1000 7.3 11 20300205 20300201 TRUE FALSE EQUALS 0

§ `Subdivision 5 -- recovery`

-- a tenant given notice under s 6.60(2)
#ASSERT `Must I pay my rent to the local government` TRUE TRUE

-- s 6.61(2)
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for not naming the owner`  EQUALS 5000

§ `Subdivision 6 -- action against the land`

-- unpaid for at least 3 years (s 6.64(1))
#ASSERT `Can the local government take possession of my land` 3
#ASSERT NOT `Can the local government take possession of my land` 2

-- more than 12 years after possession (s 6.67(1))
#ASSERT NOT `Must the local government give my land back` 13 FALSE

-- s 6.69(1)
#ASSERT `Can I stop the sale by paying` 10 EQUALS `yes, by paying the rates and the costs so far`
-- s 6.69(2)
#ASSERT `Can I stop the sale by paying` 3 EQUALS `only if the local government agrees to accept payment`

§ `Subdivision 7 -- objections`

-- s 6.76(1)(a)(i)
#ASSERT `Where does my complaint go` `the rate record names the wrong owner or occupier` TRUE EQUALS `an objection to the local government under s 6.76`
-- c055: still recorded as vacant land after handover, under differential rates (s 6.76(1)(b))
#ASSERT `Where does my complaint go` `the rate record gives my land the wrong rating category` TRUE EQUALS `an objection to the local government under s 6.76`
-- d084: a complaint about the Nedlands GRV
#ASSERT `Where does my complaint go` `my valuation is too high` TRUE EQUALS `an objection under the Valuation of Land Act 1978, not this Act (s 6.80)`
-- not a ground in s 6.76(1)
#ASSERT `Where does my complaint go` `the rate in the dollar is too high` TRUE EQUALS `no objection lies; a submission when rates are proposed (s 6.36)`
-- s 6.82(1)
#ASSERT `Where does my complaint go` `the rate was not imposed in accordance with the Act` TRUE EQUALS `a reference of a question of general interest to the State Administrative Tribunal (s 6.82)`

-- within 42 days, in writing, by the named owner (s 6.76(2), (3))
#ASSERT `Is my objection validly made` 30 FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- out of time
#ASSERT NOT `Is my objection validly made` 43 FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- time extended (s 6.76(4))
#ASSERT `Is my objection validly made` 43 TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- not the named owner or their agent or attorney
#ASSERT NOT `Is my objection validly made` 30 FALSE TRUE FALSE

-- s 6.77
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply for a review` 42 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Am I in time to apply for a review` 50 FALSE

-- s 6.81
#ASSERT `Must I still pay while my objection is decided` 

